# 高频词汇 List07
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 高频词汇List07核心词汇

{{target}}{/ˈtɑːɡɪt/}{目标；靶子}{The company set a target of 20% growth.}}
{{technique}}{/tekˈniːk/}{技术；技巧}{She mastered the technique of oil painting.}}
{{technology}}{/tekˈnɒlədʒi/}{技术；科技}{Technology has revolutionized the way we work.}}
{{temporary}}{/ˈtemprəri/}{临时的；暂时的}{This is only a temporary solution to the problem.}}
{{tendency}}{/ˈtendənsi/}{趋势；倾向}{There is a tendency for people to overeat during holidays.}}
{{term}}{/tɜːm/}{术语；学期；条款}{The president served two terms in office.}}
{{theory}}{/ˈθɪəri/}{理论；学说}{Einstein's theory of relativity changed physics.}}
{{threat}}{/θret/}{威胁；恐吓}{Cybersecurity threats are increasing worldwide.}}
{{tolerate}}{/ˈtɒləreɪt/}{容忍；忍受}{She could not tolerate his rude behavior any longer.}}
{{trace}}{/treɪs/}{追踪；痕迹}{Police traced the call to a location in the city.}}
{{tradition}}{/trəˈdɪʃn/}{传统；惯例}{This tradition has been passed down for generations.}}
{{transform}}{/trænsˈfɔːm/}{转变；改造}{Education can transform lives and communities.}}
{{transmit}}{/trænzˈmɪt/}{传输；传播}{The disease can be transmitted through contaminated water.}}
{{trend}}{/trend/}{趋势；潮流}{There is a growing trend towards remote work.}}
{{trigger}}{/ˈtrɪɡər/}{触发；引发}{The crisis triggered a wave of protests.}}
{{ultimate}}{/ˈʌltɪmət/}{最终的；极限的}{The ultimate goal is to achieve world peace.}}
{{undergo}}{/ˌʌndəˈɡəʊ/}{经历；经受}{The city underwent major reconstruction after the earthquake.}}
{{undertake}}{/ˌʌndəˈteɪk/}{承担；从事}{She undertook the challenging task with enthusiasm.}}
{{uniform}}{/ˈjuːnɪfɔːm/}{统一的；制服}{The school requires students to wear a uniform.}}
{{unique}}{/juˈniːk/}{独特的；唯一的}{Every person has unique fingerprints.}}
{{universal}}{/ˌjuːnɪˈvɜːsl/}{普遍的；全球的}{Access to clean water should be a universal right.}}
{{update}}{/ʌpˈdeɪt/}{更新；最新消息}{The software needs to be updated regularly.}}
{{urban}}{/ˈɜːbən/}{城市的；都市的}{Urban areas face increasing traffic congestion.}}
{{utilize}}{/ˈjuːtɪlaɪz/}{利用；使用}{We should utilize renewable energy sources more effectively.}}
{{valid}}{/ˈvælɪd/}{有效的；合理的}{Your passport is no longer valid.}}
{{vary}}{/ˈveəri/}{变化；不同}{Opinions vary on this controversial topic.}}
{{vast}}{/vɑːst/}{广阔的；巨大的}{The country has vast natural resources.}}
{{vehicle}}{/ˈviːəkl/}{车辆；工具}{Electric vehicles are becoming more popular.}}
{{version}}{/ˈvɜːʃn/}{版本；说法}{This is the latest version of the software.}}
{{violate}}{/ˈvaɪəleɪt/}{违反；侵犯}{The company violated environmental regulations.}}
